"overview": "Colorado's 8th District is the narrowest kind of battleground: an even partisan lean and winning margins under one point in each of the last two cycles. Republican incumbent Gabe Evans faces Democrat Manny Rutinel and Libertarian Dan Wood. Evans holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, but Democratic outside groups have poured roughly $3.5 million behind Rutinel, far outpacing support on the Republican side.\n\nRatings from ten outlets all point the same direction: none rate Evans better than a tossup, and most call the seat a Democratic lean or likely flip. Prediction markets price Rutinel's chances near 85 percent. The only public poll, from a Republican-affiliated firm in September, showed Evans ahead by two, a reminder of how close this remains. A favorable national environment gives Rutinel a modest edge in a district this evenly split.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6862, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7621, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7968, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7638, "margin": 4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8011, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8034, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7177, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7479, "margin": 4.7}]}